{"step_index":1426,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T17:28:38Z","content":"### Multi-Line Responsive Text Wrapping for Report Card Inquiries\n\n### Root Cause\nPreviously, inquiry items were wrapped in horizontal chip tags with fixed line heights and unconstrained text containers. When a teacher inquired about a complex topic (e.g. *\"Comparing FRS Pension Option 1 vs Investment Plan\"* or *\"Guaranteed 5% bonus on contributions\"*), the single-line chip exceeded the card container width and ran off the edge of the screen.\n\n---\n\n### 🎨 What Has Been Enhanced ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx) & [`LeadDetailScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx))\n\n1. **Responsive Multi-Line Checklist Layout:**\n   - Switched from rigid inline chips to an aligned, flexible checklist view (`interestsList`).\n   - Added `flex: 1`, `flexWrap: 'wrap'`, and `lineHeight: 17` to each inquiry label.\n   - Long retirement topics now wrap naturally onto 2–3 lines with generous line height and clear visual separation.\n\n2. **Handwritten Questions & Meeting Availability Callouts:**\n   - Added `alignItems: 'flex-start'` and `flexWrap: 'wrap'` to the custom handwritten question card (`customQuestionBox`).\n   - Inquiries, planning period notes, and meeting availability now respect card boundaries on all mobile viewports.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Production Deployment Live\nThe update is compiled and live on Surge:\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**"}
